{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/113126-spells-of-the-devachan-shomshak-news","id":113126,"title":"Spells of the Devachan (Shomshak news)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-14T21:35:59-07:00","id":113126,"title":"Spells of the Devachan (Shomshak news)","content":"So, turns out Shomshak's been working on stuff for the HERO system. His latest work, <a href=\"http://www.herogames.com/index.html/_/store-items/new-product-spells-of-the-devachan-pdf-r24\" target=\"_blank\">Spells of the Devachan</a>, is now on sale.<br /> <br /> Normally, Shomshak himself would be letting folk know about this, except something about his OS disagrees with the forum software here, to the tune of not letting him post threads. So, this is me (continuing) to be helpful, but expect him to chime in soonish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T00:57:55-07:00","id":113185,"title":"","content":"And here I am. Thanks again, Imrix! <br /> <br /> (I presume it's okay to post this? If not, I apologize to the Esteemed Moderators.) <br /> <br /> <i>Spells of the Devachan: Thaumaturgy from the Sorcerer's Galaxy</i> is a supplement for the superhero RPG CHAMPIONS. It's about Doctor Strange-style comic-book magic, (a subject on which I have written copiously in the past), and extends it into a new, self-contained setting of alien sorcery. <br /> <br /> There is crunch, in the form of 30+ pre-written spells, but it also features the sort of colorful and creative setting that we love from WW/Onyx Path games. Even if you don't play CHAMPIONS specifically, I hope you can find useful ideas and material to pirate for your superhero campaigns. <br /> <br /> I'll be around if anyone has further questions. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T12:36:53-07:00","id":113486,"title":"","content":"...and thus I've spent three bucks on a supplement for a game I don't (and probably won't ever) own or play, just to see Dean's take on comic book sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T22:51:37-07:00","id":113869,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Morangias! I hope you enjoy it. <br /> <br /> As mentioned, this is my <i>second</i> take on comic-book sorcery. My first was <i>The Ultimate Super-Mage,</i> (I did not pick the name), published, ye gods, 18 years ago. That was the full deal: light-show magic, weird dimensions, a Dread Dormammu/Dark Dimension homage, cosmic entities, the works. Later, HERO hired me to update it and fit it into an official &quot;CHAMPIONS Universe&quot; along with other material from other authors. You can find the results in <i>The Mystic World.</i> I still had a lot of material left over, so when HERO started licensing people to write their own supplements, I jumped at the chance. You know the Exalted &quot;extra bits&quot; products such as Splinters of the Wyld? I was going to produce a series of those. <br /> <br /> But HERO Games is now owned by a computer game company called Cryptic Studios, that wanted the CHAMPIONS Universe IP for an MMO. (Lot of that going around.) I needed Cryptic's approval to revisit my old material. At the 59th minute of the 11th hour, permission was revoked for my first supplement. I am not inclined to ask Cryptic again for anything. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, HERO's honcho Jason Walters, may the Incarnae be pleased with him, pointed out that I do not need Cryptic's permission to write supplements that do not involve the CHAMPIONS Universe. Smart guy! <br /> <br /> So I created a new universe. <br /> <br /> <i>Spells of the Devachan</i> is the first view into it. It focuses on spells and the basic cosmic framework. If sales are decent, I'll write more about the Sorcerer's Galaxy and develop some of the topics I could only allude to in this introductory work. In time I hope to hit all the classic tropes. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}